This project developed a machine learning pipeline to classify 847 metabolites into five chemical groups using HNMR spectroscopy data from the Human Metabolome Database. After binning spectra into 400 features (0.025 ppm resolution), three approaches were evaluated: two convolutional neural networks (15-23% accuracy) and Random Forest classifiers (66.4% accuracy). Feature importance analysis revealed chemically interpretable patterns: aliphatic regions (1.2-1.6 ppm) distinguished lipids, aromatic signals (6-8 ppm) identified aromatics, and alpha-to-heteroatom resonances (3.6 ppm) characterized nitrogen/oxygen-containing compounds. A Streamlit web application enables real-time classification with confidence scores, successfully validating on external spectra.